# What I Learned from the PackSmart Project

While developing PackSmart, I gained practical experience in building a web application using Python and Django. I also improved my understanding of backend development, database design, algorithms, frontend integration, and testing.

## 1. Requirement Analysis

- How to understand project requirements before starting development.
- How to divide a large project into smaller tasks.
- How to identify important business rules and possible edge cases.

## 2. Python and Django

- Creating Django models for products, boxes, orders, and order items.
- Managing database operations using Django ORM.
- Understanding model relationships, views, URLs, and service classes.
- Separating business logic from views to keep the code organized.

## 3. Database Design

- Designing database tables based on project requirements.
- Using ForeignKey relationships to connect different models.
- Applying field validation and database constraints.
- Using DecimalField for accurate storage of dimensions, weights, and prices.

## 4. Box Selection Algorithm

This was the most challenging part of the project.

- Handling six possible orientations of a product.
- Calculating total product weight based on quantity.
- Checking whether products can physically fit inside a box.
- Detecting overlapping products during placement.
- Checking the maximum weight capacity of boxes.
- Selecting the lowest-cost box that can accommodate the order.

I also understood that checking total volume alone cannot guarantee that products will fit inside a box.

## 5. API and Frontend Development

- Creating REST API endpoints using Django.
- Sending and receiving JSON data between frontend and backend.
- Using JavaScript Fetch API to communicate with Django.
- Building a warehouse dashboard using HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and Bootstrap 5.
- Handling form validation, API errors, and displaying dynamic data.

## 6. Testing and Debugging

- Writing automated test cases using Pytest.
- Testing models, APIs, and the box selection algorithm.
- Checking different product dimensions, quantities, and weight limits.
- Finding and fixing errors by comparing expected and actual results.
- Performing manual testing to verify application functionality.

## 7. Security and Code Quality

- Understanding CSRF protection and its importance.
- Learning about SQL injection and XSS risks.
- Using Django's `json_script` to safely pass data to JavaScript.
- Improving database queries to avoid unnecessary operations.
- Writing clean, reusable, and maintainable code.

## 8. Using AI Tools

- Using AI to understand requirements and plan development tasks.
- Writing prompts to get technical suggestions and code examples.
- Using AI to identify errors and explore possible solutions.
- Reviewing AI-generated code instead of accepting it directly.
- Correcting AI suggestions when they did not match the actual project requirements.

## 9. Overall Experience

This project gave me practical experience in developing a complete web application. I improved my technical skills and understood how different parts of an application work together.

The most important thing I learned is that AI can help during development, but understanding the code, checking its correctness, and taking responsibility for the final implementation are still the developer's job.